The Integration Plan
Your LZ77 outputs Vec<Triple> where Triple = (usize, usize, Option<char>). Your Huffman encodes String (bytes). You need a bridge between them.

Steps to Create DEFLATE
Serialize LZ77 output to bytes - Convert your triples into a byte stream that Huffman can encode

Design a simple format for the byte stream:

Use a flag byte to distinguish literals from back-references
For literals: [0x00][char_byte]
For back-references: [0x01][offset_high][offset_low][length_high][length_low]
For end marker (None char): [0x02]
Modify your Huffman to work with &[u8] instead of &String (or convert the byte stream to a String)

Suggested Project Structure
deflate/
├── Cargo.toml
├── src/
│   ├── main.rs
│   ├── lib.rs
│   ├── lz77/          (copy your lz77 module)
│   ├── huffman/       (copy your huffman module)
│   └── serializer.rs  (new: converts triples ↔ bytes)
Key Functions You'll Need
compress:   input → lz77_compress → serialize_triples → huffman_encode → output
decompress: input → huffman_decode → deserialize_triples → lz77_decompress → output
What to Implement
serialize_triples(Vec<Triple>) -> Vec<u8> - converts LZ77 output to bytes
deserialize_triples(Vec<u8>) -> Vec<Triple> - reverses the serialization
A deflate_compress function that chains: LZ77 → serialize → Huffman
A deflate_decompress function that chains: Huffman → deserialize → LZ77